## Provider Per Mode

Each agent mode can use a different provider or model:

```json
{
  // Chat mode provider (Conversational Q&A)
  "cursor.agent.chatProvider": "anthropic",
  "cursor.agent.chatModel": "claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
  
  // Agent mode provider (Code modification, tool execution)
  "cursor.agent.agentProvider": "anthropic",
  "cursor.agent.agentModel": "claude-opus-4-20250514",
  
  // Tab completion provider (Inline suggestions)
  "cursor.agent.tabProvider": "openai",
  "cursor.agent.tabModel": "gpt-3.5-turbo",
  
  // Plan mode provider (Analysis, strategy)
  "cursor.agent.planProvider": "anthropic",
  "cursor.agent.planModel": "claude-opus-4-20250514"
}
```

### Provider Selection Logic

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[User interacts with Cursor] --> B{Interaction type?}
    B -->|Chat/Q&A| C[Chat Provider + Model]
    B -->|Code edit/tool use| D[Agent Provider + Model]
    B -->|Inline completion| E[Tab Provider + Model]
    B -->|Planning/strategy| F[Plan Provider + Model]
    
    C --> G[Provider makes request]
    D --> G
    E --> G
    F --> G
    
    G --> H[Model processes request]
    H --> I[Response returned]
```

### Multi-Provider Strategy

Using different providers per mode optimizes for cost, speed, and capability:

| Mode | Recommended Provider | Rationale |
|------|---------------------|-----------|
| **Chat** | Anthropic (Sonnet) | Balanced reasoning and conversation |
| **Agent** | Anthropic (Opus) | Max reasoning for complex code tasks |
| **Tab** | OpenAI (GPT-3.5) | Speed-critical, lower capability needed |
| **Plan** | Anthropic (Opus) | Deep analysis requires strong reasoning |

