## Context Window Settings

The agent context window determines how much conversation history and code context the agent can process at once.

### Context Window Configuration

```json
{
  // Context window size (token count)
  "cursor.agent.contextWindow": 128000,
  
  // Maximum tokens per agent response
  "cursor.agent.maxTokens": 4096,
  
  // Context window for Tab completions (separate, smaller)
  "cursor.agent.tabContextWindow": 8192,
  
  // Enable/disable context window management
  "cursor.agent.contextManagement.enabled": true,
  
  // How much context to retain in long sessions
  "cursor.agent.contextRetention": "balanced" // "minimal", "balanced", "full"
}
```

### Context Window Modes

| Mode | Token Limit | Use Case | Performance |
|------|------------|----------|-------------|
| **Minimal** | ~8K tokens | Quick edits, focused tasks | Fastest response |
| **Balanced** | ~128K tokens | Most workflows, good context | Balanced speed/quality |
| **Full** | ~200K tokens | Large refactors, complex tasks | Slower, more context |

### How Context Is Managed

1. **Fresh context per prompt**: Each agent invocation starts fresh
2. **Conversation history retained**: Previous turns in the same Composer session are included
3. **@-references explicitly added**: Content added via `@file`, `@folder`, `@code`
4. **Open file context**: Current file content is automatically included
5. **Recent edits**: Recently modified files may be included
6. **Window limits**: When context exceeds the window, older content is compacted (see [28-context-compaction.mdc](28-context-compaction.mdc))

