## Settings Precedence

Settings are resolved in this order (highest to lowest priority):

1. **Per-prompt overrides**: Mode specified in slash command (e.g., `--plan`, `--agent`)
2. **Workspace settings**: `.vscode/settings.json` (overrides user settings)
3. **User settings**: `settings.json` in Cursor data directory
4. **Environment variables**: `CURSOR_API_KEY`, `CURSOR_MODEL`, etc.
5. **Default values**: Built-in defaults

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Slash Command Override] --> B{Present?}
    B -->|Yes| C[Use override]
    B -->|No| D{Workspace settings?}
    D -->|Yes| E[Use workspace]
    D -->|No| F{User settings?}
    F -->|Yes| G[Use user settings]
    F -->|No| H{Environment variable?}
    H -->|Yes| I[Use env var]
    H -->|No| J[Use defaults]
```

### Override Examples

```bash
# Force agent mode for this session
claude --model claude-opus-4-20250514 "Do complex refactoring"

# Force custom instructions for this prompt
claude --plan "Analyze the architecture of this service"

# Set provider via environment variable (lowest priority)
export CURSOR_PROVIDER=anthropic
export CURSOR_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514
```

